  "reviewerNote": "Four November 2011 panoramas place the plinth below the railed wood terrace. The approximately 340-degree bearing points the cutaway toward the visitor path. Across the four terrain renders, the plinth top stands 6 to 8 cm above the grade, and its underside remains below the grade. The closest mapped path clears the fitted plinth by about 11 cm. The viewer preserves all seven transportation records, the terrain and mapped water if loading fails. The original platform elevations and the current display condition remain uncertain.",
